<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frankish Kingdom</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Franks, Frankish</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Frankish Kingdom was the realm of the Franks, a Germanic people who established power in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> after the fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, first under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/merovingian-dynasty">Merovingian dynasty</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingians</a> it expanded into the Carolingian Empire, and its eastern part later became the core of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom.jpg" alt="Frankish Kingdom" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Roke · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Franks_expansion.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…separate groups across the Rhine in 406, and while Respendial's Alans saved the Vandals from defeat by the <b>Franks</b>, Goar went over to the Roman side and his followers were later settled near Orléans by the general Aetius; another group under Sambida was settled near Valence around 440.</blockquote><a href="/empire/alans">Alans · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>The end of Alemannic independence came through the rise of the <b>Franks</b>.</blockquote><a href="/empire/alemanni">Alemanni · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Moving west across the Pontic steppe, they subdued the Kutrigurs and other groups and fought the <b>Franks</b> on the Elbe, capturing the Frankish king Sigibert I in a campaign of the 560s.</blockquote><a href="/empire/avar-khaganate">Avar Khaganate · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>…Poitiers in 732 CE checked an Umayyad raid into Gaul — and Pepin the Short transformed the Carolingians from palace mayors into the effective rulers of the <b>Frankish kingdom</b>, before Pepin deposed the last Merovingian king, Childeric III, and was made king with papal approval in 751 CE.</blockquote><a href="/empire/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>After Charlemagne deposed the last Agilolfing in 788 it was governed by Frankish prefects and then became the core of the East <b>Frankish kingdom</b> of Louis the German.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-bavaria">Duchy of Bavaria · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>The emirs sent regular summer campaigns against the north: under Hisham I armies sacked Oviedo in 794 and 795 and raided Septimania in 793, though the <b>Franks</b> took Barcelona in 801.</blockquote><a href="/empire/emirate-of-cordoba">Emirate of Córdoba · Military</a></li></ul></section>
